This is Vader, an AI-native IDE built on Void (itself a fork of VS Code). Void is the deprecated upstream project this codebase was imported from.

Most Void-inherited AI code lives in src/vs/workbench/contrib/void. Vader's new agent-platform code (policy engine, permanent/temporary agents, layered instructions, MCP registry, SkillNet skill provider, browser automation, capability bus) lives alongside it under the same folder, in dedicated subfolders — see ARCHITECTURE.md for the map.

You may often need to explore the full repo to find relevant parts of code. Look for services and built-in functions that you might need to use to solve the problem.

In typescript, do NOT cast to types if not necessary. NEVER lazily cast to 'any'. Find the correct type to apply and use it.

Do not add or remove semicolons to any of my files. Just go with convention and make the least number of changes.

All types that map from a value A to B should be called bOfA. For example, if you create a hashmap that goes from toolId to toolName, it should be called toolNameOfToolId, etc.

When touching product identity, branding, or install/update metadata, keep "Vader" as the user-facing product name and preserve references to Void only where they document ancestry, licensing, or attribution (see README.md's "License and attribution" section).
